[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792777807-2042744051.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]What it does[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Every marker on the world map[/b]: spires, altars, sanctums, vaults, lairs, towns, camps, mines, caves, garrisons, quests, lore rumors, graves, and all 448 gold and 1032 silver chests.
[*][b]Mining, Materials, Plants, Bait and Trees[/b]: every ore deposit, material, plant patch and bait spot, read from the game's own world files, and every forest drawn in its tree type's colour.
[*][b]Lore Notes and Bosses[/b]: every note and diary and every boss, with the ones you've read or beaten grayed out or hidden. Return Beacons and every well and water barrel too.
[*][b]Unique gear and collectibles[/b]: every unique weapon, ring and piece of gear, the journal's collectibles (fossils, paintings, mosaic pieces...), Fell Summoning Stones and each region's night plants.
[*][b]Regions[/b]: tint each region in its own colour, or show just one (the rest dimmed or hidden) with its border drawn.
[*][b]G G: what's nearby glows[/b]: press G twice and the chests, notes and bosses near you glow through walls and floors, and the ore you track is outlined on the rock.
[*][b]A Map Key & Filters panel[/b] built from the game's own UI art: an icon, a count and an ON/OFF switch for every marker type, whole categories at a click, filters for your custom pins, and padlocks that keep a filter as you set it.
[*][b]Two more zoom steps out[/b] on the world map, and [b]Page Up / Page Down[/b] (or numpad + and -) to zoom a step at a time.
[*][b]Find on the map[/b]: press [b]Shift+F[/b], type a name or a kind of place, and the map moves to show it.
[*][b]Fog and pin modes[/b]: the game's own fog, a light fog over a fully drawn map, or no fog; and pins only where you've been, grayed out in unexplored land, or all of them.
[*][b]Looted chests[/b]: open a chest and it's hidden or grayed out with a check mark, until it comes back. Shared with other players who have the mod.
[*][b]A minimap on your HUD[/b] with the map's terrain, the time of day or the weather, and other players, that you can move, resize and zoom.
[*][b]All 15 game languages[/b]: the mod's text follows the game's language.
[*][b]Client only[/b]: works in single player, hosted games and on any dedicated server. Nothing goes on the server, and other players don't need it.
[/list]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792845210-228800814.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]The Map Key & Filters panel[/b][/size]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792845210-913068383.jpg[/img][/center]

[list]
[*][b]Every gold and silver chest in the world is included[/b]: all 448 gold chests and 1032 silver chests have their own rows in the filter, so you can show just the chests you're hunting.
[*]Click a row to show or hide that marker type.
[*][b]SHOW ALL / HIDE ALL[/b] at the top switch every marker type at once.
[*][b]REGION[/b], under them (with Settings > Advanced > Region Filter on): the arrows step through All Regions and the world's regions in level order (Springlands, Revelwood, Blackmire, Nomad Highlands, Kindlewastes, Albaneve Summits, Veilwater Basin, Cinder's Cradle); click the name to jump to the region you're in. Pins outside the region are dimmed ([b]DIM[/b]) or not shown at all ([b]HIDE[/b]), and its border is drawn as a dotted gold line. Quest pins, lore rumors and your own pins always show. Requested by VintageMarble.
[*]Click a category header to switch the whole category; [b]+ / -[/b] folds it, and it stays folded the next time you play. [b]Drag a category header[/b] up or down to move the category; the order is remembered.
[*]The rows in each category are sorted by name in your language.
[*]The mouse wheel or the scroll bar scrolls the list.
[*][b]CUSTOM PINS[/b]: click a pin icon to show or hide your own pins of that kind.
[*][b]Tab[/b] (or the - button at the top) folds the panel away; to use another key, set [i]PanelToggle=[/i] under [i][Keys][/i] in [i]minimap_config.ini[/i] (a letter, a digit, F1 to F12, CapsLock, Home, End... or None). The [b]cog[/b] opens Settings.
[*][b]Filter locks[/b]: the padlock left of a switch locks that filter. A locked filter keeps its ON or OFF through SHOW ALL / HIDE ALL, reloads and updates, and a locked category also stays open or closed; you can still click it. [b]Hold[/b] SHOW ALL or HIDE ALL to change locked filters too.
[*][b]Lore Notes[/b] (Quests & Rumors): every note and diary in the world, 574. Notes you've read are grayed out or hidden, like looted chests; unread ones are drawn bigger on an amber ring so they stand out. Hover one for its title.
[*][b]Unique Weapons[/b] and [b]Unique Equipment[/b] (World & Resources): the one-of-a-kind weapons (40, like the Wailing Blade and Talion's Bow) and rings and gear (16, like the Gemini Ring and the Flaming Gauntlets), each at the chest or place it is in, with its own icon and name. One in a gold or silver chest counts as found once that chest is looted; for the others [b]Ctrl + left click[/b] it to mark it found, saved per character. [b]Find[/b] finds them by name. Requested by Gadn.
[*][b]Collectibles[/b] (World & Resources): the journal's collectibles lying in the world, 101: fossils, skeleton pieces, the bard's paintings, Drak reliefs, mosaic pieces, meteorites and more, each with its own icon and name. [b]Ctrl + left click[/b] one to mark it found, saved per character; [b]Find[/b] finds them by name.
[*][b]Fell Summoning Stones[/b] (World & Resources): the 45 stones where Shroud Spores conjure a Fell enemy, one tier per region.
[*][b]Bosses[/b] (World & Resources): the world's bosses, named like their health bar; beaten ones are grayed out or hidden. The game keeps no record of beating some of them (the Dire Wolf, the Critter Queens, the Fog Predator...): [b]Ctrl + left click[/b] one on the map to mark it beaten or clear the mark; Ctrl + left click a beaten one to mark it not beaten (with Looted Chests: Grayed Out, beaten bosses show to click). Saved per character.
[*][b]Return Beacons[/b] (Shroud & Vaults): all 282.
[*][b]Water Source[/b] (World & Resources) also shows the world's wells and water barrels you can drink from, and the ones you build.
[/list]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792934139-1121249783.jpg[/img][/center]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792845219-1053091644.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]G G: what's nearby glows[/b][/size]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792934139-1608303195.jpg[/img][/center]

Press [b]G[/b] twice quickly while playing. For 14 seconds everything within 75 m that isn't done yet glows through walls and floors: unlooted gold and silver chests (in gold and silver), unread lore notes and bosses you haven't beaten, while their filters are on. They pulse on the world map and the minimap too, so you can see which way to go.

On the minimap, the ones 4 m or more above or below you get a green up or orange down caret, so you know whether to go up or down.

[b]Vein sight[/b]: the ore and materials of the Mining and Materials rows you have on show for 30 seconds too, for the deposits the map shows near you. Within 12 m their edges glow on the rock itself, in the game's build zone colour; dig in and the glow on the walls of your hole shows where the ore ends. Farther out (50 m) each vein is outlined on screen in its ore's colour, with the deposit's icon in its middle.

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792873369-183261406.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]Mining, Materials, Plants, Bait and Trees[/b][/size]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792866375-1531699366.jpg[/img][/center]

Read from the game's own world files, so every spot is where the game put it. Each kind has its own row in the Map Key (all off at first), and hovering an icon on the world map names it.
[list]
[*][b]MINING[/b]: every ore deposit, 21 kinds (copper, iron, silver, gold, sulfur, salt...), 7,452 in all.
[*][b]MATERIALS[/b]: farm soil, fertilised farm soil, flower soil, twigs, bones, tar, toxic slime, luminous growth, ice, gold coins, archaic essence.
[*][b]PLANTS[/b]: 30 harvestable plants, as patches, and each region's night plants (Midnight Lily, Gloomberry, Calla Luna, Shadowbloom, Glimmer Gentian, Stapelia Starflower, Passionflower, Gleam Root) where they grow at night.
[*][b]BAIT[/b]: fireflies, grasshoppers, pillbugs, frogs and more.
[*][b]TREES[/b]: each forest drawn as one shape in its tree type's colour, 18 types; the big ones carry their name.
[/list]
Deposits, materials, plants and bait also show on the minimap and in Find.

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792866375-1531293890.jpg[/img][/center]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792866380-2004491181.jpg[/img][/center]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792866380-1952592079.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]Find (Shift+F)[/b][/size]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792776528-804463773.jpg[/img][/center]

On the world map, press [b]Shift+F[/b] or click [b]FIND[/b]. Type a name or a kind of place, for example [i]gold[/i], [i]spire[/i] or [i]garrison[/i]. Every match is listed with its region, its distance from you, and [i][Locked][/i] if you haven't unlocked it yet.
[list]
[*]Click a result twice, double-click it or press [b]Enter[/b], and the map moves to show it.
[*][b]All Matching Places - Zoom to fit[/b] shows every match at once.
[*][b]F2[/b] (or [b]Ctrl+F[/b]) switches whether Find skips marker types you've hidden with the filters. Pick a result a filter hides and the Map Key opens its row and flashes it.
[*]Lore notes and bosses are found by their own names.
[*][b]Esc[/b] closes it (Shift+F types a capital F in the search).
[/list]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792777201-1180845193.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792845214-878515797.jpg[/img][/center]

The [b]cog[/b] on the Map Key (and the one under the minimap) opens Settings:
[list]
[*][b]FOG:[/b] [b]EXPLORED[/b] is the game's own fog, [b]HYBRID[/b] draws the whole map with unexplored land under a light fog, [b]REVEAL ALL[/b] has no fog.
[*][b]PINS:[/b] [b]EXPLORED[/b] shows pins only where you've been, [b]HYBRID[/b] grays out pins in unexplored land, [b]REVEAL ALL[/b] shows every pin. In every mode, a place you haven't discovered yet (the game would hide it) is grayed out, even where the fog is cleared.
[*][b]Custom Marker Size[/b]: the size of your own pins.
[*][b]Show Minimap[/b], [b]Minimap Terrain[/b] and [b]Minimap Icon[/b] (sun/moon or weather).
[*][b]Time Format[/b]: 1:00 PM or 13:00 for the minimap's clock (at first it follows Windows).
[*][b]Minimap Border[/b]: ORNATE or THIN, a fine line so the map takes less room.
[*][b]Minimap Info Bar[/b]: off hides the bar under the minimap; the cog moves to the map's bottom-left corner, and [b][[/b] and [b]][/b] still zoom. With Show Minimap off and the info bar on, the bar (time, weather, cog) stays on screen by itself.
[*][b]Looted Chests[/b]: hide them or gray them out (read lore notes and beaten bosses too).
[*][b]Completed Places[/b]: show or hide the places the game marks done, like cleared roots, used obelisks and cleared vaults, and the Flame and Night Sanctums you've visited. Shown, visited sanctums get a check mark.
[*][b]Filter Locks[/b]: how many filters are locked; [b]Remove All[/b] unlocks them.
[*][b]Advanced > Position (X, Y, Z)[/b], off at first: your position under the minimap (Y is your height) and, on the world map, the X and Z under the cursor. Click the copy button (or middle click the world map) to copy them. Requested by Loling91.
[*][b]Advanced > Region Filter[/b], off at first: the Map Key's REGION row.
[*][b]Advanced > Region Colors[/b], off at first: each region tinted in its own colour on the world map. Requested by izisot.
[/list]
Everything is remembered.

[line]

[size=4][b]Looted chests[/b][/size]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792845223-927762810.jpg[/img][/center]

Open a gold or silver chest and the mod marks it looted: hidden, or grayed out with a check mark. On the world map, [b]Ctrl + left click[/b] a chest to mark it or clear the mark. Chests you opened before installing the mod aren't known to it: they show until you open them again or Ctrl + left click them. A looted chest comes back after 30 minutes of play with every player at least 500 m away (coming closer starts the 30 minutes over), unless it's in a Flame Altar's build zone. On a dedicated server the time you're away counts too, if the server's clock kept running (one that stands still while nobody is on counts nothing). Looted chests are saved per world. Players who have the mod share them: open a chest and it's marked on their maps too.

If you open chests with another key than E, set [i]InteractKey=[/i] under [i][Chests][/i] in [i]minimap_config.ini[/i]; [i]RespawnMinutes=[/i] and [i]ResetRadius=[/i] (500 m) are there too.

[line]

[size=4][b]Minimap[/b][/size]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792845219-19805001.jpg[/img][/center]

A minimap on your HUD with the World Map's terrain, a compass, the time of day (or the weather) and its zoom level, placed under the Journal [J] tab at first. Cleared places and looted chests show a check mark. A mining or materials deposit within 75 m that is 4 m or more above or below you gets a green up or orange down caret.

[b]Hold Shift + Alt[/b] to set it up. The mouse cursor appears and the camera stops turning, so you won't swing your view or attack. While you hold them:
[list]
[*][b]Drag the minimap[/b] to move it anywhere on screen.
[*][b]Drag its bottom-right corner[/b] to make it bigger or smaller.
[*][b]Mouse wheel[/b] zooms.
[*][b]Double-click the star at the top[/b] to put it back in its default place.
[/list]
Zoom any time with [b][[/b] and [b]][/b] (or numpad - and +), or with the - / + buttons under the minimap; the [b]cog[/b] next to them opens Settings. A gold or silver chest, lore note or boss within 75 m that is 4 m or more above or below you gets a small green up or orange down caret, and so do another player and a player grave (on the world map too). [b]Other Players[/b] in the panel shows other players on the map, and on the minimap as colored arrows that point where they're heading. Position, size and zoom are saved for next time.

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792845215-1387636545.jpg[/img][/center]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/220/220-1792845223-993348796.jpg[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Close Enshrouded.
[*]Open the game folder (Steam: right-click Enshrouded > Manage > Browse local files).
[*]Copy everything from the zip into it, keeping the folders: [b]dbgcore.dll[/b] next to [i]enshrouded.exe[/i], and the [b]greeneye\unlock-map-markers[/b] folder.
[*]Start the game and open the map (M).
[/list]

[b]Servers:[/b] nothing to install. The mod only runs on your own game.

[b]Install by hand:[/b] Vortex does not know the Greeneye Loader yet.

[b]Uninstall:[/b] delete [i]greeneye\unlock-map-markers[/i]. If no other Greeneye mod is left, also delete [i]dbgcore.dll[/i] and the [i]greeneye[/i] folder.

[line]

[size=4][b]Languages[/b][/size]

The mod's text follows the game's language: English, German, French, Italian, Spanish, Portuguese (Brazil), Polish, Russian, Ukrainian, Turkish, Japanese, Korean, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese and Thai. Marker and region names come from the game itself.

To use another language, set [i]Language=[/i] in [i]greeneye\unlock-map-markers\minimap_config.ini[/i] under [i][General][/i]: [i]auto[/i] (follows the game), or [i]english, german, french, italian, spanish, brazilian, polish, russian, ukrainian, turkish, japanese, koreana, schinese, tchinese, thai[/i]. Restart the game after changing it.

The translations are my own. If something reads wrong in your language, please say so in the Posts tab.

[line]

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Single player, hosting your own game, and dedicated servers[/b], all with the mod on your game only.
[*][b]Plays well with other mods.[/b] It runs through the Greeneye Loader ([i]dbgcore.dll[/i], shared with Find, Quick Deposit, Continue and Embervale Teleport). Where another mod hooks the same game function, it chains onto that hook instead of replacing it.
[*]With the [b]Find[/b] mod installed, Find on the map uses Find's search box. G G uses the same glow as Find and Quick Deposit, and all three work together.
[*][b]Safe on game updates.[/b] Made for the current game version. If an update changes code the mod patches, it skips that part instead of crashing, and the log says so.
[*]Works with Steam. Not tested with other store versions.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]

If something doesn't work, please post these files with your report. Both are in the game folder:
[list]
[*][i]greeneye\unlock-map-markers\unlock_map_markers.log[/i]: what the mod found and patched.
[*][i]greeneye\loader.log[/i]: what the Greeneye Loader did.
[/list]
[b]Ctrl + Shift + F12[/b] switches the whole mod off and on, to compare with the game as it is (best with the world map open).

[line]

[size=4][b]Changelog[/b][/size]

[b]1.3.15[/b]
[list]
[*]Fixed: the fog mode (Explored / Hybrid / Reveal All) went back to Explored every time you started the game. Reported by Gadn.
[*]Fixed: Revelwood's Abandoned Farms and Abandoned Windmills, which the game never puts on the map, showed grayed out for good. They stay hidden now, like in the vanilla game. Reported by BlaineCraner.
[*]Fixed: a section's ON / OFF stayed ON when one of its rows was locked ON. The switch now changes every row in its section, locked rows too; Show All / Hide All still leave locked rows alone.
[/list]

[b]1.3.14[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Unique Weapons[/b] (40) and [b]Unique Equipment[/b] (16): every one-of-a-kind weapon, ring and piece of gear at the chest or place it is in, with its own icon and name; found once its chest is looted, or [b]Ctrl + left click[/b] to mark it found. Requested by Gadn.
[*][b]Collectibles[/b] (101): the journal's fossils, skeleton pieces, the bard's paintings, Drak reliefs, mosaic pieces, meteorites and more, each with its own icon and name. Requested by TheSefer and BlaineCraner.
[*][b]Fell Summoning Stones[/b] (45): where Shroud Spores conjure a Fell enemy, one tier per region.
[*][b]Night plants[/b]: each region's plants that grow only at night (Midnight Lily, Gloomberry, Calla Luna, Glimmer Gentian, Stapelia Starflower, Passionflower, Gleam Root, and Shadowbloom's night spots).
[*][b]Settings > Advanced > Region Filter[/b] (off at first): a Region row in the Map Key shows one region, the others dimmed or hidden, with its border drawn. Requested by VintageMarble.
[*][b]Settings > Advanced > Region Colors[/b] (off at first): each region tinted in its own colour on the world map. Requested by izisot.
[*][b]Settings > Advanced > Position[/b] (off at first): your X, Y and Z under the minimap, the X and Z under the cursor on the world map, and a button to copy them. Requested by Loling91.
[*][b]G G vein sight[/b]: the ore of the Mining and Materials rows you have on is outlined for 30 seconds, on the rock itself within 12 m and on screen out to 50 m.
[*]On the minimap, a mining or materials deposit 4 m or more above or below you gets the up or down caret.
[*]A boss and the unique item in its chest are drawn side by side, so either can be hovered and clicked.
[*]Fixed: the mod's icons showed on top of a marker's menu (Fast Travel / Send Ping / Set as Waypoint).
[*]Fixed: typing a capital F into a custom pin's name opened Find and closed the name box. Reported by dremen.
[*]The new rows and settings start off.
[/list]

[b]1.3.13[/b]
[list]
[*]Folded Map Key categories stay folded the next time you play. Requested by HadToRegister.
[*][b]Ctrl + left click[/b] works on every boss: a beaten one can be marked not beaten (with Looted Chests: Grayed Out they show to click). Requested by Delacroix.
[*]Places you haven't discovered yet are grayed out, even where the fog is cleared, so you can tell which ones you still have to find. Requested by Delacroix.
[*]On a dedicated server, a lore note you read hides right away, from what the server sends, instead of after the server saves.
[*]On a dedicated server, time away only brings chests back if the server's clock kept running: one that stands still while nobody is on no longer clears your looted chests.
[/list]

[b]1.3.12[/b]
[list]
[*]The key that folds the Map Key panel can be changed: [i]PanelToggle=[/i] under [i][Keys][/i] in [i]minimap_config.ini[/i] (Tab at first; None for no key). Requested by KazarusKain.
[*]Bosses the game keeps no record of beating (the Dire Wolf, the Critter Queens, the Fog Predator and others): [b]Ctrl + left click[/b] one on the map to mark it beaten.
[*]A player grave 4 m or more above or below you gets the up or down caret, on the minimap and the world map.
[/list]

[b]1.3.11[/b]
[list]
[*]World map: [b]Page Up / Page Down[/b] (or numpad + and -) zoom in and out one step.
[*]Map Key: drag a category header to move the category; the rows in each category are sorted by name in your language. Water Source moved to World & Resources.
[*]Settings > [b]Time Format[/b]: 1:00 PM or 13:00 for the minimap's clock. Requested by Kriiks.
[*]Unread lore notes are drawn bigger on an amber ring so they stand out, and Flame and Night Sanctums you've visited get a check mark (hidden with Completed Places: HIDE). Requested by TheSefer.
[*]Minimap: another player 4 m or more above or below you gets the up or down caret.
[*]Reported bugs fixed: the active quest's marker (like the Crucible) hid under Fog: EXPLORED (reported by HadToRegister); Shift+F closed Find while typing a capital F, and typing it into the game's text boxes (like a pin's name) opened Find (reported by HadToRegister); the Fog Dragon didn't show as beaten.
[/list]

[b]1.3.10[/b]
[list]
